Z||000000||shanestacy||06-19-2001||08:37 PM||||I have a 1986 Fiero GT V-6, 4-speed Muncie manual transmission.  The VSS shaft and gear broke off in the transmission.  I bought a new VSS and blue gear but I'm not sure which way to install the blue gear on the VSS shaft.  Does the blue gear go on gear first, or shaft first?  I'm not having any luck either way.  The speedometer still reads 0 all the time.  I checked all the fuses and connections.  I also jacked the car up, had someone put it in gear so I could watch the natural colored gear inside the transmission, and it turned.  After it cooled off, I put my finger in there and the natural colored gear does not feel stripped.  Any other ideas?  Please HELP me!||||reg||8
